{comment: Chorus}
[G]It is joy unspeakable and full of glory,
[D]Full of glory, [G]full of glory;
It is joy unspeakable and full of glory,
Oh, the [Am7]half has [D7]never yet been [G]told.[C][G]

{comment: Verse 1}
[G]I have found His grace is [C]all comp[G]lete,
He [D]supplieth my every [D7]need;
While I [G]sit and learn at [C]Jesus' [G]feet,
I am [D]free, yes, free [D7]indeed.

{comment: Verse 2}
[G]I have found the pleasure [C]I once [G]craved,
It is [D]joy and peace wi[D7]thin;
What a [G]wondrous blessing [C]I am [G]saved
From the [D]awful gulf of [D7]sin.

{comment: Verse 3}
[G]I have found that hope so [C]bright and [G]clear,
Living [D]in the realm of [D7]grace;
Oh, the [G]Savior's presence [C]is so [G]near,
I can [D]see His smiling [D7]face.

{comment: Verse 4}
[G]I have found the joy no [C]tongue can [G]tell,
How its [D]waves of glory [D7]roll!
It is [G]like a great o'er[C]flowing [G]well,
Springing [D]up within my [D7]soul.
